{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_ptxwbt4bss4b5crp3q3pngsk6xklxzxwnpfufoeo6exlw6yg3znq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. All four phases passed the completion gate.\n\n## What I found\n\nThe translation was structurally complete (all 20 symbols present, all 4 data tables byte-identical) but had **9 real correctness bugs**, all the same class: the Rust passed the wrong operand as the SSE *destination*.\n\n`mulss dst, src` returns the *quieted destination* when the destination is NaN, and only otherwise the source. So `mulss(a,b)` and `mulss(b,a)` return **different NaN payloads** while agreeing on every non-NaN input — invisible to happy-path tests. I read the correct operand roles straight out of `objdump -d` on the C `.so` (which `CMakeLists.txt` builds at `-O0`, so the codegen is fixed).\n\n| # | function | fix |\n|---|----------|-----|\n| 1 | `c2Dot` | y-term's `mulss` dst is `b.y`, and the final `addss` dst is the y-term |\n| 2 | `c2CircletoCircle` | `addss` dst is `B.r`, not `A.r` |\n| 3 | `f9` | five hand-inlined, individually-wrong dot products → one shared `lm_dot2` matching the C |\n| 4–6 | `f9` denom/`u`/`v` | `mulss` dsts are `dot00`, `dot01`, `dot00`/`dot01` |\n| 7 | `f11` `m` | GCC folds `1.0f *` away entirely — the extra `mulss` was spurious |\n| 8 | `f11` arms 3–6 | four stores had `addss(m, x)`; the C always makes `x`/`c` the dst |\n| 9 | `f13` | `mulss` dst is the `60.0f` literal; `addss` dst is `360.0f` |\n\nReproducer for #1: `c2Dot({0x7FC00000, 0x7FC00000}, {0xFFC00000, 0xFFC00000})` → C gives `0xFFC00000`, Rust gave `0x7FC00000`.\n\nI also had to correct **two of my own `ERRORS.md` claims** after running the C: `f3(INT_MIN, -1)` is `INT_MIN` (not `1` — the `+1` overflows `INT_MAX`), and `f3` is *not* floored division when `v1 ≥ 0 && v2 < 0`, because `r = v1 % -v2` is never negative so the fix-up can't fire — `f3(7, -2) == -3`, not `-4`. The Rust already reproduced that quirk correctly; my documentation was wrong, so I fixed the doc, not the code.\n\n## Artifacts (`translation/`)\n\n- `SYMBOLS.md` — 20/20 symbols, 0 missing, 0 extra, 0 undefined non-libc, verified for **both** release and debug `.so`\n- `ERRORS.md` — 36 rows; 35 have passing tests, E36 (dereferenced NULL) is genuine UB in the C and documented rather than asserted\n- `CONFIGS.md` — 64 rows; 62 have dedicated tests, C63/C64 are the build-config rows\n- `FIXES.md` — the 9 fixes plus an explicit list of what I verified as *already correct* (e.g. `agglom`'s reversed `addsd` operand order is unobservable because the `isnan()` guards mean the value operand is never NaN)\n- `run_tests.sh`, ~5,200 lines of tests\n\n## Results\n\n**432 passing test executions** (108 tests × release/dev × default/no-default-features), plus a fuzz soak at **40,000,000 iterations per function** with zero divergences. Verified from a clean slate (`rm -rf c_src/build translation/target`).\n\nTwo things worth flagging:\n\n1. **`cargo test` alone does not rebuild the `.so` under test.** Because the crate is `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]` only, the integration tests have no cargo dependency on it — so `cargo test` happily runs against a stale `libagglom_lib.so`. This bit me once (a fix appeared not to work). `run_tests.sh` always does `cargo build` first; if you invoke cargo by hand, do the same.\n2. **The NaN-payload fidelity is tied to the C being built at `-O0`.** That is what the given build command produces, and the pre-existing `addss`/`mulss` helpers show it was the intent. If the C were rebuilt at `-O2`, GCC would commute some of these operations and a few of the 9 fixes would need re-deriving from the new disassembly.\n\nI also added `libloading = \"0.8\"` to `[dev-dependencies]` and a `.cargo/config.toml` with `offline = true`, since crates.io was unreachable through the proxy but the crate was already in the local registry cache. Nothing in `c_src/` was touched (mtimes and line counts confirmed unchanged)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1185,"cache_read_input_tokens":282846,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1185,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3c626898-bd76-4a29-9454-b5abc5e34b9c","uuid":"fe04eed1-11c0-4e2b-bdea-8a8d9b7673bf","timestamp":"2026-08-27T04:40:50.417Z"}
